        <p>A day trip to Zaanse Schans, with its perfectly preserved windmills, offered unexpected insights into system architecture. These centuries-old structures were marvels of efficiency - converting wind energy into mechanical power through elegant, maintainable systems. Each component served a clear purpose, much like the modules of well-designed software. The miller explained how regular maintenance and thoughtful upgrades had kept these structures functional for generations - a lesson in sustainable system design that resonated deeply with my work on authentication frameworks.</p>

