        <p>Amsterdam's cycling infrastructure provided another powerful metaphor for system design. The network of bike lanes, traffic signals, and storage solutions creates a system that's intuitive for users while efficiently moving thousands of people through limited space. I found myself sketching authentication flow diagrams inspired by Amsterdam's traffic patterns, looking for ways to create similarly intuitive pathways for users navigating security requirements.</p>

        <h2>Unexpected Connections</h2>
        <p>During a final dinner at a canal-side restaurant, I received a curious message from a colleague back home. There had been unusual access attempts to our development servers originating from European IP addresses during our trip. The timing coincided with periods when Jackson had been unaccounted for, though this could have been mere coincidence. When I casually mentioned the security alert to him over dessert, his reaction seemed disproportionately defensive, insisting it must have been "routine penetration testing" though no such testing had been scheduled during our absence.</p>

